# One finding ID per line (CVE, GHSA, AVD-DS-*, secret rule, license).
# Optional expiry suffix: ' exp:YYYY-MM-DD'. Audited suppressions carry a
# statement in docs/operations.md.
#
# Every entry was enumerated from a Trivy v0.75.0 scan of the published
# firmware-tools digest on 2026-10-03 (vuln+secret+misconfig, CRITICAL/HIGH);
# see docs/operations.md "Container hardening" for the full analysis.
#
# --- cryptography 46.0.7 vendored inside PlatformIO/ESP-IDF ---------------
# Two vendored copies ship in the image:
#   opt/platformio/packages/tool-esptoolpy/_contrib/  (esptool's bundled
#     Python contrib — esptool needs it for secure-boot/signing at runtime)
#   opt/platformio/penv/.espidf-6.1.0/                (ESP-IDF helper venv,
#     created by idf_tools at build warm-up)
# Both track the pinned espressif32 platform / ESP-IDF release, not this
# repo's uv.lock; the fixed cryptography (48.0.1/49.0.0/50.0.0) only lands
# when upstream re-vendors. The image runs gates with --network none, so
# the packages are not reachable as a network surface. Re-evaluate at the
# next ESPRESSIF32_PLATFORM / ESP-QEMU bump — deferral recorded in
# scripts/dependency_update_deferrals.json.
CVE-2026-69247 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-69249 exp:2027-01-03
GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- urllib3 1.26.20 vendored inside the ESP-IDF helper venv ---------------
# opt/platformio/penv/.espidf-6.1.0 ships urllib3 1.26.20 for idf_tools.py
# downloads; the version is fixed by the pinned ESP-IDF release. Gates run
# with --network none so idf_tools never fetches at runtime; stripping it
# would break the toolchain. Same deferral as the cryptography group.
CVE-2025-66418 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2025-66471 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-21441 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-44431 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- Example Dockerfiles inside vendored ESP-IDF ---------------------------
# DS-0002 (root USER) and DS-0029 (missing --no-install-recommends) fire on
# upstream example Dockerfiles shipped inside
# opt/platformio/packages/framework-espidf/ (openthread environment,
# harness-simulation posix, tools/docker). They are documentation-grade
# upstream files, never built by this repo; the findings clear when the
# pinned ESP-IDF release refreshes. Same deferral.
AVD-DS-0002 exp:2027-01-03
AVD-DS-0029 exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- Test private keys inside vendored ESP-IDF -----------------------------
# 354 private-key findings, all under opt/platformio/packages/framework-
# espidf/: mbedtls tf-psa-crypto/openthread test vectors (data_files/*.key,
# *.pem) and tcat_ble_client sample commissioner/device certs. These are
# upstream-published test fixtures, not credentials. Waiving the rule is
# accepted with the same deferral; a real key committed outside the
# vendored tree would need a new scanner signal, so the waiver expires
# with the others rather than standing permanently.
private-key exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- Unfixable HIGHs in the QEMU/Ubuntu and Python payload -----------------
# qemu-system-arm/-common/-data plus the ubuntu-helper-virt-hwe and
# ubuntu-virt metapackages carry CVE-2026-3886 (HIGH) with no released
# fix, and the Python `ecdsa` package vendored in the toolchain's helper
# venvs carries CVE-2024-23342 (HIGH) — the publish gate's ignore-unfixed
# already passes them, so they are recorded here as deliberate, expiring
# acceptances rather than ambient findings. Re-evaluate at each
# ubuntu:26.04 base-digest and ESPRESSIF32_PLATFORM / ESP-QEMU bump.
CVE-2026-3886 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2024-23342 exp:2027-01-03

